#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# dirac_comb

#% text
# `dirac_comb(x)` represents the Dirac comb, the sum of `dirac_delta(x - k)` over the integers `k`; `dirac_comb(x1, ..., xk)` is the product of the combs in each argument.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# At a real number that is not an integer the value is 0; at integers and symbols it stays unevaluated.

#% item
# The comb is even: a negated argument is replaced by its negation.

#% item
# Lists are mapped elementwise.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
dirac_comb(1/2)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
[dirac_comb(0), dirac_comb(factorial(10))]
#% output
#= [dirac_comb(0), dirac_comb(3628800)]

#% cell
dirac_comb(4, 8, 1/3)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
dirac_comb([-0.5, 0, 0.5])
#% output
#= [0, dirac_comb(0), 0]

#% cell
dirac_comb(-x)
#% output
#= dirac_comb(x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `dirac_delta`, `fourier_transform`
